  "body": "Check 2D and 3D Adaptive (Trochoidal) clean-up passes against the cutter radial engagement limit across every `max_engagement` setting (including the 90.0 deg default).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- **Checked clean-up ladder (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch_clean.rs`, `adaptive_troch.rs`, `adaptive_troch_level.rs`, `machining3d/troch.rs`)**:\n  - Factored clean-up peeling into `plan_cleanup_step` and added `plan_cleanup_checked`, which carves a single-level stock with the planned lanes and measures clean-up passes against `t.max_engagement` using `quality::measure` whenever clean-up chains are emitted.\n  - When baseline clean-up exceeds `t.max_engagement`, steps down the peel step along `CLEANUP_LADDER` (`1.0, 0.75, 0.5, 0.35, 0.25`) until engagement fits within the limit, noting the reduction on the toolpath.\n  - If even the finest ladder step still exceeds `t.max_engagement`, emits a named note via `cleanup_engagement_note` (`CLEANUP_ENGAGEMENT_NOTE_PREFIX`) instead of silently overloading the cutter or dropping the 90.0 deg default check.\n  - Wired `plan_cleanup_checked` into both `adaptive_troch.rs` (2D, removing the `max_engagement != DEFAULT_MAX_ENGAGEMENT` skip) and `adaptive_troch_level.rs` / `machining3d/troch.rs` (3D).\n- **Advisory operation & status-line warning (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`, `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, `crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`, `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`)**:\n  - Added advisory `Warning::EngagementExceeded { at, measured_deg, limit_deg }` (`blocks_post() == false`), promoted from `cleanup_engagement_exceeded(&path.notes)` in `generate.rs`, exposed via MCP as `\"engagement_exceeded\"`, and rendered on its own UI status-line warning group.\n- **Tests (`crates/motion/tests/adaptive_troch_clean.rs`, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch_tests.rs`, `crates/app/tests/adaptive_trochoid.rs`, `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`)**:\n  - Pinned default `90.0 deg` and custom `60.0 deg` (`wide 30x24 D6` and `L-shape D10`, which previously hit `64.0` and `62.5 deg` in clean-up on `main`) under `adaptive_troch_clean`.\n  - Verified `plan_cleanup_checked` reports `exceeded` when even step-down cannot hold a tight limit, round-trips 2D/3D note parsing, promotes to advisory `Warning::EngagementExceeded`, and surfaces cleanly on the UI status line.\n  - Preserved all existing 2D/3D trochoidal golden CL files byte-identically.\n\n### Verification (on `b0169b4d1b8b7934ebdd9c67a245667c5420117c`)\nAll verification ran in software and simulation tests (not on a mill):\n- `cargo clippy -j 10 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass (exit 0)\n- `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-motion --test adaptive_troch_clean`: 2 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-app --test adaptive_trochoid --test pocket3d_trochoid`: 18 passed, 0 failed (`adaptive_trochoid` 13, `pocket3d_trochoid` 5)\n- `cargo test -j 10 -p camcraft-ui --lib --test operations -- --test-threads=1`: 1,682 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored (`lib` 1,651, `operations` 31)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off`): 322 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (5,142 passed, 0 failed, 113 ignored across `sim`, `motion`, `app`, `ui`)\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (11 passed, 0 failed)\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree upstream/main HEAD`: clean (exit 0)\n\nfork synced at v0.26.0\nChangelog: Checked 2D and 3D Adaptive (Trochoidal) clean-up passes against the engagement limit with automatic step-down and a named advisory warning.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3849",
